{"actor": "unknown-agent", "data": {"documentation_gaps": {}, "duration_s": 25.9, "landed_paths": 0, "missing_artifacts": 0, "next": "Extend E209 entrant measurement to additional PSC codes to test whether the bimodal pattern generalizes beyond the top 5 codes", "outcome": "worked", "push_requested": false, "summary": "E209 prototype screen completed and verified against committed E209 raw data. Prototype classifies 5 federal IT PSC codes: 3 enterable (DA01, DA10, 7A21) with active newcomer entry and balanced turnover, 2 closed shops (7030, D304) with zero newcomers and exit-only dynamics. Key finding: DIF (turnover balance) distinguishes enterable from closed-shop codes, not fragmentation. Bimodal pattern confirmed. Next: extend entrant measurement to additional PSC codes to test generalizability of the bimodal pattern.", "unlogged_changes": 14}, "host": "instance-20260717-0944", "kind": "session_end", "schema": "origin.session.event/1", "seq": 17, "session": "2026-10-21-010-build-e209-prototype-screen-for-federal", "ts": "2026-10-21T10:44:35+00:00"}
